    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.content }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "/no_think\n\nYou are a metadata extractor. Output ONLY a JSON object wrapped in `json` code fence. No prose, no thinking, no explanation before or after.                                   \n                                                          \nRequired fields:\n- title (string)\n- summary (string, max 200 chars)\n- domain (one of: tech, science, business, health, philosophy, misc)\n- type (one of: concept, entity, pattern, guide, decision)\n- tags (array, max 5 short lowercase strings)\n- entities (array, max 3 proper nouns)\n- key_claims (array, max 3 strings)\n- provenance (always \"extracted\")\n\nExample output:\n```json\n{\"title\":\"...\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"domain\":\"tech\",\"type\":\"concept\",\"tags\":[\"a\",\"b\"],\"entities\":[],\"key_claims\":[\"...\"],\"provenance\":\"extracted\"}\n```\n\nNever invent info. Extract only from the source text."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        448,
        0
      ],
      "id": "47ab6c5e-a1b8-4411-8ae7-071dee768fa3",
      "name": "extract-metadata"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const files = $input.first().json.files || [];\nif (files.length === 0) return [];\nreturn files.map(f => ({json: {clip_path: f}}));"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "id": "5a72a1d2-9d1a-48ac-9b51-0b3b4b7fc199",
      "name": "split-clips"
    },
